<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Combat of the Thirty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1351">1351</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-breton-succession">War of the Breton Succession</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Combat of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> was an arranged fight on 26 March 1351, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-breton-succession">War of the Breton Succession</a>, between thirty knights and squires from each side. Champions of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-of-blois">Charles of Blois</a> led by Jean de Beaumanoir met men of the Anglo-Breton garrison of Ploërmel under Robert Bemborough at a site between Josselin and Ploërmel. The Franco-Breton side won, and the fight became a celebrated example of chivalry.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/combat-of-the-thirty.jpg" alt="Combat of the Thirty" width="320" height="171" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Octave Penguilly L'Haridon · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Le_Combat_des_Trente_(1857).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
